(This brief only changes `Free` for a buffer. A list literal is HEAP_ALLOC'd
 and registered in the heap table, so `HEAP_FREE` already released it before
 this fix - unchanged here. Its after-state is not the buffer contract
 (empty + refused writes): master-measured on 0.4.13, `Print items` after
 `Free items` still prints the list's old contents - the header's memory is
 released but the variable's slot still holds the stale pointer, and
 nothing has overwritten that freed page yet. Documented honestly as
 today's behaviour, not changed by this brief.)

a list called items is [1, 2, 3].
Free items.
Print items.
Print "len {items's length}".
